      <memberdef kind="function" id="classQfMapCanvas_1a631ef3b9dd18516083c5bdab69594835" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void QfMapCanvas::freeze</definition>
        <argsstring>(id)</argsstring>
        <name>freeze</name>
        <qualifiedname>QfMapCanvas::freeze</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>id</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Freezes the map canvas refreshes.</para>
<para>In case of repeated geometry changes (animated resizes, pinch, pan...) triggering refreshes all the time can cause severe performance impacts.</para>
<para>If freeze is called, an internal counter is incremented and only when the counter is 0, refreshes will happen. It is therefore important to call <ref refid="classQfMapCanvas_1a631ef3b9dd18516083c5bdab69594835" kindref="member">freeze()</ref> and unfreeze() exactly the same number of times. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="src/core/qml/QfMapCanvas.qml" line="91" column="6"/>
      </memberdef>
